O`. I'll also add the green LED, `D1`, with its current-limiting resistor, `R121` (1.0k), and the `J6` jumper for the power indicator.\n\nBefore I can proceed, I'll need to define some new nets. `USB2ANY_3.3V` and `CVDD_CO` need to be declared, since they are used for the isolator power and aren't yet defined. I'll also define `J6` as a jumper.\n\nHere's my plan for the next iteration: First, I will declare the new nets: `USB2ANY_3.3V`, `CVDD_CO`, and `POWER_IND`. Then, I'll instantiate `C57` and `C58`, as well as `D1`, `R121`, and `J6`. Next I will route the connections. I will connect `C57` to `USB2ANY_3.3V` and GND, and `C58` to `CVDD_CO` and GND.\n\nFor the LED indicator circuit, I'll connect `D1` and `R121` appropriately. Since SCUD indicates that `J6` acts as a power indicator, I'll connect it in series with the LED, between `VCC` and the LED circuit. I am assuming that `VCC` is the overall power rail for the indicator. So, the connections will be: `VCC` to `J6`, then from `J6` to `R121`, and then `D1` to GND.\n\nFinally, I'll add connections for `CVDD` to `CVDD_CO` via `J18`, a 2-pin header. I'll declare the `CVDD_CO` net. Then, I will instantiate `J18` and then connect `CVDD` to one pin of `J18` and `CVDD_CO` to the other pin of `J18`. \n", 'signature': None}], 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_e1eb3fc431bb4dc99ccfc2740445', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'file_editor', 'arguments': '{"command": "str_replace", "path": "/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/output/bq79616_circuit.tsx", "old_str": "      <net name=\\"CB16\\" />\\n\\n      {/* U1: BQ79616PAPQ1 (Main BMS IC) */}", "security_risk": "LOW", "new_str": "      <net name=\\"CB16\\" />\\n\\n      {/* New Nets for Isolator Power and Power Indicator */}\\n      <net name=\\"USB2ANY_3_3V\\" />\\n      <net name=\\"CVDD_CO\\" />\\n      <net name=\\"POWER_IND\\" />\\n\\n      {/* U1: BQ79616PAPQ1 (Main BMS IC) */}"}'}}]}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'The file /home/p