                             test points), and their connections as described in the SCUD.\n\nNow, I will focus on implementing the \"Temperature Measurement                    
                             Subsystem\" as described in the SCUD. This involves:\n\n1.  **Reference Power:** `TSREF` connected to `PULLUP` via `J5`.\n2.  **Divider             
                             Network:** 8 parallel voltage dividers, each with a 10.0k pull-up resistor (R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19) and an NTC thermistor             
                             (RT1-RT8) to GND.\n3.  **Measurement Points:** The midpoint of each divider (`GPIOx_R`).\n4.  **GPIO Interface (J4):** Connecting BMS               
                             `GPIOx` pins to `GPIOx_R` via J4.\n5.  **Channel 1 Filter:** Special filter for `GPIO1_R` consisting of R128, C60, and D3.\n6.  **DNP               
                             Components:** R20 (100k) and C12 (DNP) on RT8 channel.\n\n**Plan for next iteration:**\n\n1.  Declare new nets: `PULLUP`, `GPIO1_R`,                
                             `GPIO2_R`, ..., `GPIO8_R`, `GPIO1_C`.\n2.  Instantiate `J5` (2-pin header).\n3.  Instantiate pull-up resistors `R7, R8, R11, R14, R15,              
                             R16, R18, R19` (10.0k).\n4.  Instantiate thermistors `RT1-RT8` (NCP18XH103F03RB).\n5.  Instantiate `R128` (1.0k), `C60` (1uF), `D3`                 
                             (BZX84C24).\n6.  Instantiate `J4` (2x8 Header).\n7.  Instantiate `R20` (100k) and `C12` (0.1uF, DNP).\n8.  Connect `TSREF` to `PULLUP`              
                             via `J5`.\n9.  Connect the pull-up resistors and thermistors to form the voltage dividers, connecting their midpoints to `GPIOx_R`                  
                             nets.\n10. Connect `GPIO1_R` to `GPIO1_C` via `R128` and filter with `C60`, `D3`.\n11. Connect `GPIOx_R` (or `GPIO1_C` for channel 1)               
                             to `J4`.\n12. Connect U1's `GPIO1` through `GPIO8` pins to the respective pins on `J4`.\n13. Instantiate `TP44` and connect it to                   
                             `GPIO1_R`.",                                                                                                                                        
