                                     "text": "I've completed the implementation of the NPN power supply circuit, connecting             
                             Q1, R3, R4, and C1 according to the SCUD.\n\nNext, I will implement the Cell Balance (CB)                  
                             Configuration Path and the Voltage Sense (VC) Configuration Path. These involve a set of 0-ohm             
                             resistors (R21, R22, R25, R26 for CB and R23, R24, R27, R28 for VC) that are currently DNP (Do             
                             Not Populate). Even though they are DNP, their connections are specified. I will instantiate               
                             them and define their connections.\n\nFrom SCUD:\n**Cell Balance (CB) Configuration Path:**\n*             
                             `R25` connects `CB12` to `CB13`\n*   `R21` connects `CB13` to `CB14`\n*   `R26` connects                   
                             `CB14` to `CB15`\n*   `R22` connects `CB15` to `CB16`\n\n**Voltage Sense (VC) Configuration                
                             Path:**\n*   `R27` connects `VC12` to `VC13`\n*   `R23` connects `VC13` to `VC14`\n*   `R28`               
                             connects `VC14` to `VC15`\n*   `R24` connects `VC15` to `VC16`\n\nI will also connect the                  
                             respective `CBx` and `VCx` pins of U1 to their corresponding nets.\n\n**Plan for next                      
                             iteration:**\n\n1.  Instantiate `R21, R22, R25, R26, R23, R24, R27, R28` as 0-ohm                          
                             resistors.\n2.  Connect these resistors to the appropriate `CBx` and `VCx` nets.\n3.  Connect              
                             U1's `CB0` to `CB16` pins to their respective nets.\n4.  Connect U1's `VC0` to `VC16` pins to              
                             their respective nets.\n    *Note: The SCUD explicitly mentions connections for `CB12` to                  
                             `CB16` and `VC12` to `VC16`. For the remaining `CBx` and `VCx` pins (0-11), I will connect                 
                             them to their respective nets for completeness, assuming they are routed to these nets within              
                             the IC.*",                                                                                                 
