are critical, especially J17, J21, and J2.
5.  **Jumper implementation.** For each jumper (J1, J2, J3, J4, J5, J6, J17, J18, J21), instantiate it and connect it according to the 
SCUD and pin numbers.
6.  **U1 Connections.** Now, for the main IC, U1. Power supplies (BAT, AVDD, CVDD, DVDD, etc.) and ground (AVSS, CVSS, DVSS, etc.). Then
the cell inputs (VC0-VC16) and the balancing circuits (CB0-CB16), the GPIOs to the temperature sensing, and finally the communication 
pins.
7.  **The NPN power supply.** Get Q1, R3, R4, and C1 connected correctly.
8.  **Cell Count Configuration.** Those DNP 0-ohm resistors (R21, R22, etc.) for cell count must be spot on to properly set up the VC 
and CB lines.
9.  **Auxiliary Measurement Inputs.** R9, R12, C10, R10, R13, C11, R17 for the Bus Bar and current sense. Also, don't forget the test 
points TP16, TP17, TP18, TP19.
10. **Temperature Measurement.** R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19, RT1-RT8, R128, C60, D3, R20, C12. Get the GPIO1 filter right. 
Don't forget J5, J4, voltage dividers, and TP44.
11. **Power indicator implementation.** D1, R121, J6 to POWER\_IND.
12. **The Test Points.** I will wrap it up by putting in the rest of the test points, connecting them all to their nets. (TP1-TP9, 
TP13-TP15, TP10, TP11).

