.pin2" to="net.GND" />\n   203\t\n   204\t      <trace from="net.CVDD_CO" to=".C58 > .pin1" />\n   205\t      <trace from=".C58 > .pin2" to="net.GND" />\n   206\t\n   207\t      {/* Connections for Power Indicator */}\n   208\t      <trace from="net.POWER_IND" to=".J6 > .pin1" />\n   209\t      <trace from=".J6 > .pin2" to=".R121 > .pin1" />\n   210\t      <trace from=".R121 > .pin2" to=".D1 > .cathode" />\n   211\t      <trace from=".D1 > .anode" to="net.GND" />\n   212\t\n   213\t    </board>\n   214\t  );\n   215\t}\n   216\t\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected. Edit the file again if necessary.'}], 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_549c8b82a2b342cf982dd0434333', 'name': 'file_editor'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'thinking_blocks': [{'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': 'Alright, time to tackle the Auxiliary Measurement Components. I\'ve already got the Cell Balance, Voltage Sense, and the isolator and power indicator circuitry down. Now, I\'m moving on to the crucial auxiliary inputs: BBP and BBN, the positive and negative sides of the current sensing.\n\nBased on the SCUD, I have two paths to consider: the bus bar measurement path, which is currently "Do Not Populate" (DNP), and the active current sense path.\n\nSo, here\'s what I\'ll do:\n\n1.  **Define the Nets:** First, I\'ll create the necessary nets: `BBP_CELL`, `BBN_CELL`, `SRP_S`, `SRN_S`, `BBP`, and `BBN`. These are fundamental to the auxiliary measurements, and it is crucial that the nets are properly named in the schematic as they are critical to the measurement function of the design.\n\n2.  **Bus Bar Filter:** For the bus bar path (Path 1), I\'ll add the differential RC filter: `R9`, `R12` (402-ohm resistors), and `C10` (0.47μF capacitor). I\'ll also include the DNP (Do Not Populate) resistors `R10` and `R13` (0-ohm resistors) for the connection to the U1. It’s important to have these components in the schematic, even if they aren\'t populated, so it\'s clear what the design intent was 