ncing, and auxiliary measurements.\n- Input filter components (R5, C5).\n- NPN supply components (R4, R3, C1).\n- Internal regulator decoupling capacitors (C6, C9, C7, C8, C59, C3, C2).\n- Cell Balance (CB) and Voltage Sense (VC) configuration path resistors (R21, R22, R23, R24, R25, R26, R27, R28).\n- Auxiliary measurement components (R9, R12, C10, R10, R13, C11, R17) and test points (TP16, TP17, TP18, TP19).\n- Temperature sensing subsystem components: Jumper J5, pull-up resistors (R7, R8, R11, R14, R15, R16, R18, R19), thermistors (RT1-RT8), GPIO1 filter components (R128, C60, D3), Jumper J4, DNP components (R20, C12), and Test Point TP44.\n- Communication interface components: Jumpers J17, J18, J21, J1, J2, J3, and test points (TP12, TP42, TP43).\n- All necessary connections between these components and nets as detailed in the SCUD document.\n\nMy task is complete.'}], 'role': 'assistant'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "The previously generated `tscircuit` `.tsx` file (bq79616_circuit.tsx) requires significant corrections based on human feedback.\n\nPlease re-evaluate the circuit generation with particular attention to the following:\n1.  **ISO7342 Connections:** Ensure all connections and components related to the ISO7342 digital isolator (U2) are correctly implemented.\n2.  **Jumper Implementation:** Accurately include all specified jumpers (e.g., J17, J18, J21, J1, J2, J3, J4, J5) and their connections as per the SCUD and schematic images. They appear to have been largely ignored in the previous attempt.\n3.  **Schematic Image Reference:** Strictly refer to the schematic images located at '/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana_worker/resources/schematic_images' for visual clarification and accurate circuit construction. Use the SCUD file at '/home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana_worker/resources/bq79616_eval_board.scud' as the primary source of information.\n\nThe goal is to generate a complete and 